WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.482
One innocent loop

00:00:01.293 --> 00:00:02.331
can hide O

00:00:02.166 --> 00:00:03.911
N squared complexity

00:00:04.446 --> 00:00:05.354
The code works

00:00:05.165 --> 00:00:06.580
instantly for 100

00:00:06.392 --> 00:00:07.170
messages

00:00:07.253 --> 00:00:08.042
but run it

00:00:07.854 --> 00:00:09.516
on 100,000 and

00:00:09.328 --> 00:00:10.920
it becomes agonizingly

00:00:10.731 --> 00:00:11.344
slow

00:00:11.557 --> 00:00:12.924
taking seconds or

00:00:12.878 --> 00:00:13.785
even minutes for

00:00:13.597 --> 00:00:14.339
work that should

00:00:14.151 --> 00:00:15.389
take milliseconds

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:17.077
Python strings are

00:00:16.889 --> 00:00:18.362
immutable so every

00:00:18.174 --> 00:00:19.683
plus-equals allocates

00:00:19.495 --> 00:00:20.461
a new block

00:00:20.615 --> 00:00:21.593
copies the whole

00:00:21.405 --> 00:00:22.112
report

00:00:22.325 --> 00:00:23.468
appends the message

00:00:23.351 --> 00:00:24.683
and discards the

00:00:24.518 --> 00:00:25.391
old string

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:27.549
By iteration 10,000

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.296
it copies 9,999

00:00:30.108 --> 00:00:31.452
characters before adding

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:31.959
one more

00:00:32.219 --> 00:00:33.079
so doubling the

00:00:32.891 --> 00:00:34.152
messages quadruples

00:00:33.964 --> 00:00:34.660
the time

00:00:34.896 --> 00:00:35.709
the fix is

00:00:35.521 --> 00:00:36.334
to collect them

00:00:36.146 --> 00:00:36.959
in a list

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:37.749
and join them

00:00:38.286 --> 00:00:39.300
Full story on

00:00:39.111 --> 00:00:40.007
the dashboard
